    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **23 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the `registrationDate` year, e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is purely derived from the owner's own fields, I followed the existing pattern for the other derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than adding a pipeline step or persisted column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes `customerCode + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`.\n\nThe expression is null-safe (returns `null` when `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent), which matters because the seed owners in `data.sql` have neither field set \u2014 without the guard, listing/fetching seed owners would NPE. The value flows through both `POST /api/owners` (create response) and `GET /api/owners/{id}` since both map via `toOwnerDto`.",
